Subject: [PATCH 11019/11171] Record an unstamped CRITICAL, and the boundary of
 what I checked

experiment_6973 reads as live-CRITICAL with no flagged_adversarial stamp, caught
by summarize_artifact's own gap warning. Its verdict_class is partial and it has
no status.

Established: _log_experiment_completion returns on a verdict rejection about two
lines before it calls _check_auroc_anomaly, so a verdict-rejected task does not
reach the post-completion detectors.

Not established, and recorded as not established: where flagged_adversarial is
actually stamped. Line 3502 only reads it. Whether stamping shares that early
return is unverified.

Also recorded because it nearly became a false negative: my first corpus scan
for other instances was guarded on hasattr(av, "verify_artifact_file"), which is
false, so it silently produced an empty result that would have read as "no other
cases". Same guarded-call mistake as earlier in this session. Caught before
reporting, and it is why the corpus question stays open rather than answered.

It matters if systematic: an artifact that earns a CRITICAL and never gets
stamped is invisible to every consumer filtering on flagged_adversarial,
including capstones and evidence tables, which is the one thing the fabrication
gate exists to prevent.

Closes with the positive half. REQ-CONDUCTOR-VERDICT-3 fired correctly in
production for the first time: the 10:15Z FAIL reads artifact_verdict_not_terminal
where it would previously have claimed the artifact was never written.

